Anthony, 2026-10-25: "Go with your suggestion". The suggestion was the first process tool under integrated-flo's 83d2b0775fe79af6:dec:idea-a-few-core-tools-each-running-a-process-of-subtools (b + c), serving job 4 of reflow2:dec:idea-reflow2-does-fewer-things-and-does-them-really-well ("Show whether what was built meets what was asked, by checks anyone can re-run"), built in the same reflow2 PR as dec:a-fix-names-the-findings-it-answers-in-the-same-call. One call does, in order:
- the passing verification (and IMPLEMENTS from its test files);
- the change record, with `answers` naming the findings it closes;
- the changed files' accepted checksums, and the artifacts they register;
- the capability or decision marked built.
Each step gets its own receipt, and a refused step names itself and writes nothing. The tools it composes stay served for the unusual case. The pattern is measured: agents ran add_change_event then set_artifact_checksums 129 times, and verification, change, checksums, then artifact or mark-built 16 times in full (83d2b0775fe79af6:fact:the-processes-people-and-agents-repeat-most-2026-10-25).
